{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q124079930","formula":"BiO⁺","hill":"BiO","elements":["O","Bi"],"composition":{"O":1.0,"Bi":1.0},"names":{"en":"Bismuthyl","ru":"Висмутил"},"descriptions":{"en":"Bismuthyl is an inorganic oxygen-containing singly charged ion with the chemical formula BiO+. In inorganic chemistry bismuthyl has been used to describe compounds such as BiOCl which were assumed to contain the bismuthyl cation, and it was also presumed to exist in aqueous solution. This diatomic ion is not now believed to exist.","ru":"Висмути́л (англ. Bismuthyl, Bismuthyle) — неорганический кислородсодержащий радикал, однозарядный ион с химической формулой BiO+, представляет собой оксикатион висмута в степени окисления +3. Чаще всего образуется при гидролизе солей трёхвалентного висмута, прежде всего, нитрата, хлорида и других галогенидов."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":5237718,"mass":224.98,"charge":1,"smiles":"O=[Bi+]","inchikey":"AFQPDONMRFOLIJ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"oxobismuthanylium","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"5237718","atoms":2,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.95,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.95,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Bi"}],"bonds":[[0,1,2.0]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q124079930","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bismuthyl_%28ion%29","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%92%D0%B8%D1%81%D0%BC%D1%83%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BB","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/5237718","license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},{"role":"structure","name":"RDKit","url":null,"licen